{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>יפיפית</b> — Some say it is duplicated, like שחרחרת and סחרחר, for diminishment; לבנה אדמדמת, because it is not fully red. If so, how can יפיפית be for diminishment?! The answer: the duplication of the ayin and the lamed is for diminishment; only the peh and the ayin, which are duplicated, come for increase. The proof is תשגשגי, which is more than תשגי." "<b>יפיפית</b> — In His form and appearance." "<b>הוצק חן</b> — From the root of ויצקו על העולה, as though grace was poured into His mouth. So it explicitly recounts the form of His body and His speech, that it is beautiful; and by way of allegory it tells of His soul, that it is upright, and of His wisdom, that it is broad — for inner speech is found in the soul of man."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:51.940873633Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}